    "question": "Has the bot actually reduced the per-trade loss rate on historical XAUUSDT data?",
    "direct_answer": "NO_STATISTICALLY_PROVEN_LOSS_RATE_REDUCTION",
    "summary": "1) A1 (V17.9.2 SL/TP baseline) has 139 closed independent episodes (7 wins / 132 losses, loss rate 94.96%, 95% Wilson CI [90.02%, 97.52%], modeled net PnL -$282.49). 2) D1 (Macro + Unicorn + V17.9.2 SL/TP) has 16 closed independent episodes (1 win / 15 losses, loss rate 93.75%, 95% Wilson CI [71.67%, 98.89%], modeled net PnL -$31.69) plus 4 open-at-horizon censored episodes. D1 reduced total dollar loss by 88.8% (-$282.49 -> -$31.69) by filtering out 88.5% of trade volume (139 -> 16 closed episodes), NOT by materially lowering the per-trade loss rate (-1.21 percentage points delta, well inside wide confidence intervals). 3) D2 (Macro + Unicorn + MTF FULL) has only 2 closed independent episodes (1 win in DEV, 1 loss in OOS; loss rate 50.00%, 95% Wilson CI [9.45%, 90.55%], modeled net PnL +$2.74). With n=2 closed trades, D2 is severely underpowered (INCONCLUSIVE) and cannot be claimed as a sustainable 50% loss rate."
  },
